{"author":{"id":"e0b5a45ee94df92761e1991b03f72f45cac91cde564e2faac1223bf52a3fe292"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788195536,"nonce":"4WgYL4pgsMtGy8T12uqPjd2QWUU=","message":"CLOSED — verified in-game on BORGES against `_RimWorld-Agent`, all four phases,\nacross three builds. Merged to main at `24e5f7a`; DLL at `8d4ff00`.\n\nThe orchestrator ran every phase personally. The numbers below are re-derived\nfrom the raw result envelopes, not from the runner's summary line.\n\n\nOne-line repro build (`makingFor = prevMakingFor`), TWO fresh fixture benches,\nclock stopped throughout:\n\n    R4  N1 - T0 = 594     (fixture 1)\n    R4  N1 - T0 = 555     (fixture 2)\n    R5  tick still 1015 both times — the write was the verb, not the clock\n    R3b no DoBills* entry in either list — defect 4 visible in the same run\n\nBoth inside `ReCheckFailedBillTicksRange` = `IntRange(500,600)`. **Two fixtures,\ntwo different values** is the RNG-burn evidence the acceptance calls for — the\ndraw is `Rand.RangeInclusive` off the shared stream.\n\n\nSame map both times: the fixture was saved to `autostart.rws` at tick 607 and\nboth builds booted it, so this is a genuine before/after rather than two\ndifferent colonies.\n\n    main    total=0  available_total=0  blocked_total=0   no DoBills* entry\n    branch  total=1  available_total=0  blocked_total=1\n\n    branch blocked[0]:\n      work    \"DoBillsButcherFlesh\"\n      label   \"prioritize butcher at wooden butcher table\"\n      reason  \"Missing 1x corpses\"\n      job_def null\n\nM3 holds exactly: `blocked_total` 0 -\u003e 1, higher by precisely the one giver that\ngained a reason.\n\n**`total=0` on main is the CORRECT baseline, not a fixture miss**, and it is\nworth stating because it looks like one. `StartOrResumeBillJob`'s two arms are\nmutually exclusive — `if (makingFor != pawn) { nextTickToSearchForIngredients = ... }\nelse if (flag) { JobFailReason.Is(\"MissingMaterials\"...) }`. main takes the write\narm and sets no reason, so `ScanWorkGivers`' `if (!JobFailReason.HaveReason)\ncontinue;` drops the giver entirely. `ShouldSkip` does not gate this away: it\nreturns false as soon as any bill giver on the map has `AnyShouldDoNow`, which\nthe fixture bill satisfies. So the giver is reached on both builds and the two\nruns are one `if` apart.\n\n\n    F.2b  ingredient_search_cooldown = 0 on a fresh bill\n    F.4a  next_ingredient_search_tick IDENTICAL to N0 after orders\n    F.6   still identical after a SECOND orders call\n    F.6c  tick 1133 unchanged across the whole phase\n    F.7   red_error count = 0\n    F.8   no `action` journal row for orders\n    F.5   note no longer carries \"Read-only: no job is taken.\"; it discloses\n          the bill deletion, the job-id consumption AND the paused-flag rewrite\n\n\nRun on main's DLL and on the branch's, same result both times:\n\n    D1  paused_stored=false  current_count=19..37\n    D2  one orders call\n    D3  paused_stored=TRUE, state=\"paused\"\n\nClock stopped between D1 and D3, so nothing but `orders` could have moved it.\nA scribed field, written by the verb that used to call itself read-only.\n\n\n19 checks, 0 failures, M+F+D, after the merge and the `Build:` commit — so the\ncommitted DLL is the one that was verified, not merely one built from the same\nsource.\n\n\n- **The RNG burn's downstream effect.** Two deltas in the window prove the draw\n  happened. Proving it desynced anything needs a paired-run determinism harness\n  that does not exist here.\n- **The danger-threshold divergence (consequence 3).** Not tested. No fixture was\n  built where a target is reachable at `Deadly` and unreachable at `Some`. What\n  is shown is that the flag is now set for the whole scan.\n- **Third-party work givers.** 32 mod dirs on this bench; nothing here audits\n  their `JobOnThing` implementations. That is why the cost is disclosed in the\n  header rather than declared absent.\n- **Phase M's `blocked_total` comparison** was made across two bench sessions on\n  the same saved map, not within one process.\n\n\n`accept/32b9e01-orders-makingfor.ps1` (`1bf2913`) — raw file protocol in\nPowerShell, since BORGES has no python. `-Build main|branch|repro` selects the\nassertions AND is checked against the loaded assembly before anything is\nmeasured (`next_ingredient_search_tick` exists only post-fix, so it identifies\nthe binary directly).\n\n**It found two of its own bugs, and that is the argument for keeping the raw\nenvelopes.** It reported M2 and F.5 as FAILURES when the branch was right: the\ngiver defName is `DoBillsButcherFlesh`, not the `DoBillsButcherTable` guessed\nfrom the building's def; and a case-insensitive `/Read-only/` search matched the\nnew note's own phrase \"asking is **not** read-only\". Both were caught by reading\n`.accept-evidence/` rather than the summary.\n\n\nEach one produced a run that would otherwise have passed for the wrong reason:\n\n1. **`world-fixture {steps:[\"bench\",\"bill\"]}` does not chain.** Filed separately.\n2. **F4 is a radius test, not map-wide.** A corpse 53 cells out is not in play.\n3. **`total=0` on main is expected** (above).\n4. **Phase D needs a warm `resourceCounter`.** `CountProducts` counts stockpiled\n   things only and rebuilds on a TICK, so with the game paused it stays 0 forever;\n   and `ButcherCorpseFlesh` / `Make_StoneBlocksAny` have no fixed product so their\n   counter is 0 regardless. A stove's `CookMealSimple` works. Warm the counter,\n   THEN add the bill — a bill that exists while the clock runs gets its flag\n   flipped by an ordinary think tick and leaves `orders` nothing to prove.","files":null}]}